item.description:
Look closely and you&#039;ll see how much more nutritious kale is over pac choy, except for fola (folic acid) where pac choy beat kale hands down. The moral of this is the importance of some variety. Each food has its strong points. It is just that kale has so many strong points! By the way, I left the RDA column amount in as a reference, but the comparison is just between 3.5oz (100g.) of kale and pac choy. It should be said too that pac choy is a mighty healthy vegi. It just looks weak when judged against kale. 

Now, speaking of availability in the market. I happened to see kale at the market last year and was blown away by the price. As I recall they charged close to $5 a bunch (about a plant). It is easy to be a rich person if you measure wealth in how much kale you can grow. It is the easiest and most prolific. So why do they charge so much? I suppose it is just a case of supply and demand. Little demand makes for little supply which increases the price for those rare persons who buy kale. Interesting.

